==Enemy==
Henry is a backliner with Long Distance attacks, high health and relatively low damage, able to perma-freeze any unit caught in his AoE with near-perfect uptime. Henry's coverage is extremely wide, so getting units inside his large blind spot or breaking them from the freeze proves difficult without special tactics.

==Strategy==
Henry freezes your attackers by abusing your meatshields as stepping stones so other enemies could easily steamroll through them, making him a powerful support unit. He does have a minimum range, so if you can get your cats in a good position, you've basically already won. Another strategy is to lure him to the [[Cat Base]], as not as many cats will be frozen due to [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] standing at their minimum effective range, and he doesn't deal much damage to the base. If there's an opening, rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can deal massive damage to him, as his standing range is well within Henry's blind spot, although some other short-ranged units can also work, as long as they're fast enough. Do take note that Henry will still attack if there is something in his standing range, including his blind spot.

[[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Units that are immune to freeze]] such as [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] are great against Henry. [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] can utilize its freeze immunity to enter Henry's blind spot and freeze Henry, possibly allowing your units to escape, if you time him right. It is recommended to use these units in most encounters with Henry. These units aside, you might be able to use Curseblast on him just before he can attack, shutting down his ability for a few seconds and freeing any stuck units.

Since Henry's time between attacks is only slightly longer than his freeze duration, any unit with a small bit of investment in freeze resistance will have a chance to move forward. Upgrading the [[Ototo Corps#Foundation and Style Upgrades|Thunderbolt Style]] reduces the freeze uptime of Henry and any other [[:Category:Enemies with Freeze ability|freezing enemies]] that may be in the stage by a maximum of 15%.

